  "answer_text": "The next NBA game is **Game 3 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **San Antonio Spurs** and the **New York Knicks**. \n\nBecause the Knicks won the first two games on the road in San Antonio to take a 2-0 lead, the series is shifting to New York. \n\n### **Next Game Details:**\n* **Matchup:** San Antonio Spurs at New York Knicks (Game 3)\n* **Date & Time:** Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET\n* **Location:** Madison Square Garden, New York, NY\n\n---\n\n### **Where to Buy Tickets:**\n\nSince this is the NBA Finals at Madison Square Garden with the Knicks chasing their first championship in over 50 years, tickets are in extremely high demand. You can secure tickets through several official and verified secondary marketplaces:\n\n1. **Ticketmaster (Official Partner):** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and Madison Square Garden, Ticketmaster is the safest place to find verified primary and fan-to-fan resale tickets.\n2. **NBATickets.com:** The official portal run by the NBA redirects you to authorized tickets and team-specific resale markets.\n3. **Major Secondary Marketplaces:** If the official inventory is sold out, you can find a wide variety of resale tickets on trusted platforms like:\n   * **SeatGeek** (which serves as a major secondary marketplace with \"deal score\" ratings)\n   * **StubHub**\n   * **Vivid Seats**\n   * **TickPick** (known for having no hidden buyer fees)\n\n### **What to Expect on Price:**\nDue to the historic nature of this series, \"get-in\" prices (for upper-deck seating) are starting around **$1,100 to $1,850+**, while lower-level tickets are running anywhere from **$3,500 to over $7,500**. Be sure to compare prices across different resale sites to find the best deal, and always verify that the platform offers a buyer guarantee.",
